WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.233
This crosswalk is the
reference you'll come back to,

2
00:00:03.233 --> 00:00:06.568
the store table seen by object
type: every object type,

3
00:00:06.568 --> 00:00:10.812
the store its attributes live in,
who writes them and what reads them.

4
00:00:10.812 --> 00:00:14.224
Users, devices, Arc servers
and service principals

5
00:00:14.224 --> 00:00:17.637
each have their own stores
and their own consumers.

6
00:00:17.637 --> 00:00:19.612
The highpoint is the third column.

7
00:00:19.612 --> 00:00:23.318
Every row names one writer,
whether that's HR provisioning,

8
00:00:23.318 --> 00:00:27.563
device registration, the Arc agent
or an attribute administrator.

9
00:00:27.563 --> 00:00:30.931
That's the same single-writer
rule we set for the user schema,

10
00:00:30.931 --> 00:00:32.237
applied to everything.

11
00:00:32.237 --> 00:00:35.500
And one user row leads straight into PIV.
